      },
      "message": "fix(verify): the stock source is judged unless the user marks it raw stock only\n\nReview of PR #1097 reproduced a real gouge posting under the inferred\nrule (a stock made from the part plus any unrelated model an op\ntouches). The inference is gone: a from-model stock's source model\nleaves the program verdict only when the user ticks \"The source model\nis raw stock only (not judged as the part)\" - SetStockSourceOnly, one\nundo step, with the MCP tool set_raw_stock_only, a stock page\ncheckbox and an optional project-file key (absent = false). Off is the\ndefault, so every document judges as before. An op that names the\nmodel (source or boundary pick) puts it back; a mark that leaves\nnothing to judge refuses by name; a gouge on the stock's source says\nwhere the setting is. Pinned by the review's two reproductions.\n\nFixes #1094\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
